# ============================================================
# Cevano IT Solutions — Cloudflare Pages redirects configuration
# ============================================================
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# This site's canonical URLs (sitemap.xml, <link rel="canonical">, Open
# Graph tags) all use the www subdomain: https://www.cevano.co.uk
#
# The rule below 301-redirects the bare apex domain to www, so both
# cevano.co.uk and www.cevano.co.uk work, but only one canonical version
# is ever indexed by search engines. This requires BOTH cevano.co.uk and
# www.cevano.co.uk to be added as Custom Domains on the Cloudflare Pages
# project (see README-deployment.md, "Connecting the custom domain").
#
# If you'd rather have the bare apex (cevano.co.uk, no www) be canonical
# instead, delete the rule below and let me know — the canonical tags,
# sitemap, and Open Graph URLs across every page would need updating to
# match, since they're generated from a single SITE_URL constant in
# build.py.

https://cevano.co.uk/*  https://www.cevano.co.uk/:splat  301!
